From b63ba37c3cb8f239383ce1aae4433f27b6c4c9bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:35:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(03-39): change a document type as a new version

- migration 0317: rag_begin_document_version gains p_force_new_version (skips the file-hash skip, resumes only the same type); rag_get_document_for_type_change and rag_admin_document_scope for the operation
- changeDocumentType re-runs ingest() on the same identity from the stored original; the stored parse output is reused with no parser call when it serves the new profile, otherwise the original is parsed again
- the forced-version state is saved with the run, so a resume does not turn into a content duplicate; only changeDocumentType sets it
- scopeForAdminDocument mints the document own tenant scope for the tenants the admin administers, null for any other id

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
